+
+## Request
+
+Users report surprising `applyPatch` results: patches they consider invalid are accepted, edge cases
+give unexpected results, and failures do not behave as RFC 6902 reads. Review and make behaviour conform.
+
+## Done
+
+- The whole patch is validated before any operation is applied (`op`/`path` own string members,
+  `value` for add/replace/test, `from` for move/copy, known op, well-formed pointers).
+- `replace` now replaces in place, keeping object member order (it used to remove then re-add).
+- Tests added; `node --test` passes. A failing patch throws and leaves the input untouched.
